   "source": [
    "## 4. Inverse folding\n",
    "\n",
    "The backbone is held fixed and resampled to the input at every step; only the sequence and side\n",
    "chains are drawn afresh. This is a special case of partial diffusion and cannot be combined with\n",
    "its parameters."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0810e85",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Settings — sampling temperature\n",
    "\n",
    "`IF_TEMPERATURE` scales the noise injected during sequence sampling\n",
    "(`local_latents` `sc_scale_noise`). Lower values give sequences that repeat; higher values give\n",
    "more diverse ones. The config default is `0.1`; we raise it to `1.5` here to sample a more\n",
    "varied set of sequences for the same backbone, and lower it again when a conservative redesign\n",
    "is wanted.\n",
    "\n",
    "Setting it to `0` does not give deterministic sampling: it removes the noise but keeps the\n",
    "drift, and the result collapses. Use `gt.mode: ode` for that."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "af548a59",
