   "source": [
    "## 5. Partial diffusion\n",
    "\n",
    "The design is re-noised to a point part-way along the trajectory and diffused back. Unlike\n",
    "inverse folding, both modalities are resampled, so the backbone moves as well — this is a local\n",
    "search around an existing solution rather than a pure sequence redesign."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b748c463",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Settings — how much to change\n",
    "\n",
    "`PARTIAL_FRACTION` is the fraction of the trajectory to re-run, and the only parameter needed\n",
    "here: larger values change the design more, approaching de novo generation as it tends to 1.\n",
    "\n",
    "The advanced per-modality controls (`partial_t_backbone`, `partial_t_latent`,\n",
    "`couple_partial_t`) are mutually exclusive with this one and are covered in the guide."
   ]
  },
